WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
When I'm marking practice answers, I check the verbs first,

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.300
because they show straight away whether the grammar is under control.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.600
Let's fix one sentence, then link two trends.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.600
Here's the sentence. "The share of electric cars rise sharply after 2018

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.500
and now it is going to reach 45%."

6
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.900
Can you find the problems?

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.200
First, the recorded part. After 2018 has already been recorded,

8
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.900
so we need the past simple: rose, not rise.

9
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.200
Second, the projected part. We need a future form,

10
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:50.600
and we need to say when: is expected to reach 45% by 2030.

11
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.200
Third, drop "now".

12
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.300
It mixes two time frames in one sentence.

13
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.000
So: "The share of electric cars rose sharply after 2018,

14
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.100
and it is expected to reach 45% by 2030."

15
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.700
Now, linking. On the commuting graph,

16
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.600
cycling went up and car use went down.

17
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:20.600
To join two opposite trends in one sentence, use while or whereas.

18
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.600
"While cycling rose, car use fell."

19
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.100
Or: "Car use fell, whereas cycling rose."

20
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.000
If you'd rather start a new sentence,

21
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.600
use However, In contrast or By contrast at the start, followed by a comma.

22
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.900
When you check your own writing, start with the verbs too.

23
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.600
On the right page there are four sentences about the commuting graph,

24
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.000
each with one mistake.

25
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:59.100
Fix them, then write one sentence that links the two trends.
